    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the key difference between IS:710 Marine Plywood and IS:303 BWR Plywood?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "IS:710 Marine Plywood uses unextended Phenol Formaldehyde synthetic resin adhesive and can withstand 72 hours in boiling water without delaminating. IS:303 BWR (Boiling Water Resistant) withstands up to 8 hours in boiling water. Marine ply is strictly required for sink units, bathroom vanities, and coastal homes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is HDHMR better than Marine Plywood for modular kitchens?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "HDHMR (High Density High Moisture Resistance) is excellent for kitchen shutters and CNC grooved panels due to its zero-void uniform density. However, for internal kitchen carcasses and sink units prone to pipe leaks, calibrated 16mm or 19mm IS:710 Marine Plywood remains superior in load-bearing screw retention and long-term water immersion resistance."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What is the standard price per sq ft for IS:710 Marine Plywood in Mumbai and Navi Mumbai?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In 2026, 16mm and 19mm IS:710 certified marine grade plywood ranges between ₹115 and ₹175 per sq ft for branded options (CenturyPly Club Prime, Greenply Marine, Austin Gold), and ₹85 to ₹110 per sq ft for semi-branded calibrated core plywood."
